      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I ran it with the following command line options:\n\u003e `--target\u003d\"x86_64-darwin13-gcc\" --as\u003dyasm --enable-static --enable-pic --enable-vp8 --enable-postproc`\n\u003e \n\u003e I am currently using an Apple M4 Pro, and the compiler and macOS SDK information are as follows.\n\u003e ❯ clang -v\n\u003e Apple clang version 17.0.0 (clang-1700.0.13.5)\n\u003e Target: arm64-apple-darwin24.3.0\n\u003e Thread model: posix\n\u003e InstalledDir: /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Toolchains/XcodeDefault.xctoolchain/usr/bin\n\u003e \n\u003e ❯ xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-version\n\u003e 15.5\n\u003e \n\u003e If necessary, I can share `configure.log`.\n\nThanks for the detail. I see the following with Xcode 16.4 (`Apple clang version 17.0.0 (clang-1700.0.13.5)`)\n\n## Before\n\n```\n$ ../configure --enable-ccache --target\u003d\"x86_64-darwin13-gcc\" --enable-static --enable-pic --enable-vp8 --enable-postproc\n  enabling ccache\n  enabling pic\n  enabling vp8\n  enabling postproc\n  enabling vp9_encoder\n  enabling vp9_decoder\nConfiguring for target \u0027x86_64-darwin13-gcc\u0027\n  enabling x86_64\n  enabling runtime_cpu_detect\n    disabling avx512: not supported by compiler\n  using yasm\n  enabling unit_tests\n  enabling webm_io\n  enabling libyuv\nCreating makefiles for x86_64-darwin13-gcc libs\nCreating makefiles for x86_64-darwin13-gcc examples\nCreating makefiles for x86_64-darwin13-gcc tools\nCreating makefiles for x86_64-darwin13-gcc docs\n```\n\n## After\n\n```\n$ ../configure --enable-ccache --target\u003d\"x86_64-darwin13-gcc\" --enable-static --enable-pic --enable-vp8 --enable-postproc\n  enabling ccache\n  enabling pic\n  enabling vp8\n  enabling postproc\n  enabling vp9_encoder\n  enabling vp9_decoder\nConfiguring for target \u0027x86_64-darwin13-gcc\u0027\n  enabling x86_64\n  enabling runtime_cpu_detect\n  enabling mmx\n  enabling sse\n  enabling sse2\n  enabling sse3\n  enabling ssse3\n  enabling sse4_1\n  enabling avx\n  enabling avx2\n  enabling avx512\n  using yasm\n  enabling unit_tests\n  enabling webm_io\n  enabling libyuv\nCreating makefiles for x86_64-darwin13-gcc libs\nCreating makefiles for x86_64-darwin13-gcc examples\nCreating makefiles for x86_64-darwin13-gcc tools\nCreating makefiles for x86_64-darwin13-gcc docs\n```\n\nThe first output is a little misleading as all x86 optimizations are removed.",
